{
  // The maintenance Worker. **It is never deployed.**
  //
  // It exists so that the two jobs nobody can do from the outside — answering a
  // deletion request, and looking at what the archive store actually holds —
  // have one written-down tool instead of a scratch file rebuilt from memory
  // each time. Wrangler has no way to list or delete R2 objects, and the
  // service itself deliberately has no delete route: a public endpoint that
  // removes somebody's archive is a liability, and the promise in the privacy
  // policy is answered by a person reading an issue, not by a stranger's HTTP
  // request.
  //
  // So it runs locally against the real bucket and nowhere else:
  //
  //   npx wrangler dev --remote --config server/maintenance/wrangler.jsonc --port 8799
  //
  // `--remote` is what binds it to the live bucket; without it the binding is a
  // local simulation and every answer is about nothing. Authentication is the
  // wrangler login of whoever runs it, which is why there is no key in here and
  // no route below: the only way to reach it is to be the person who started
  // it, on their own machine.
  //
  // `workers_dev` and the absent `routes` are both deliberate. A deploy of this
  // file would put an unauthenticated delete endpoint on the public internet.
  "name": "efferent-maintenance",
  "main": "index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-28",
  "workers_dev": false,
  "r2_buckets": [
    {
      "binding": "BLOBS",
      "bucket_name": "efferent"
    }
  ]
}
